# "Any number of targets" includes zero (CR 115.1d; Fireball's ruling: "You may cast Fireball with zero targets, regardless
# of the value chosen for X ... no damage will actually be dealt"). Bot1 casts Fireball with X = 2 and no target: it costs
# {2}{R} (no target beyond the first), all three red floated are spent, and nobody is dealt damage.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Fireball
Mountain x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Fireball.Cast(X: 2)
Bot1.Target()

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Damage = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Fireball; Black Lotus
